<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04SN">Construction <span data-tag="04SN">10.1.6.22</span> <span class="named">(Decalage)</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $X_{\bullet }$ be a simplicial object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. We let $\operatorname{Dec}_{+}( X )_{\bullet }$ denote the augmented simplicial object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ given by the composition </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{+}^{\operatorname{op}} ) \xrightarrow { \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(C^{\operatorname{op}}_{+}) } \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{\mathrm{min}}^{\operatorname{op}} ) \subset \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}^{\operatorname{op}} ) \xrightarrow { X_{\bullet } } \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \]
</div>
<p> where $C_{+}$ denote the concatenation functor of Remark <a data-tag="04S8" href="/tag/04S8">10.1.6.2</a>. We will refer to $\operatorname{Dec}_{+}(X)_{\bullet }$ as the <em>augmented decalage</em> of $X_{\bullet }$. We let $\operatorname{Dec}(X)_{\bullet }$ denote the underlying simplicial object of $\operatorname{Dec}_{+}(X)_{\bullet }$, given by the composition </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}^{\operatorname{op}} ) \xrightarrow { \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(C^{\operatorname{op}}) } \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{\mathrm{min}}^{\operatorname{op}} ) \subset \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}^{\operatorname{op}} ) \xrightarrow { X_{\bullet } } \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}. \]
</div>
<p> We will refer to $\operatorname{Dec}(X)_{\bullet }$ as the <em>decalage</em> of $X_{\bullet }$. </p>
